WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.968
-Welcome, welcome, welcome,
everyone. Welcome to --

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.033
-Love you, Jimmy!
-I love you, too.

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:05.634
I really do.

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:07.767
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."
You're here.

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:10.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
You made it.

00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:12.067
That sounds good.

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:13.734
Well, guys,
here's some good news.

00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:16.834
Today President Biden said that
he wants states to open up

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:20.133
vaccines to all adults by
April 19th,

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:23.000
nearly two weeks sooner
than his initial goal.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:30.701
Or as Biden calls it,
Operation Early Bird Special.

00:00:30.701 --> 00:00:33.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:35.100
You know
more people are vaccinated

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.300
when pajamas sales go down
and Spanx go up.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:42.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:43.734
Yeah, this is exciting.

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:46.634
Hopefully if we're
all vaccinated on 4/19,

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:48.701
we'll be passing
something else on 4/20.

00:00:48.701 --> 00:00:50.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
Hey, what?

00:00:50.434 --> 00:00:52.167
Oh, whoa, whoa, whoa.
What does that mean?

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:54.801
Oh, hey.
-Hey. Come on.

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:58.934
-I read that 40% of adults in
the U.S. have been vaccinated.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:01.167
So now when you see
someone without a mask,

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:04.334
it's a fun game of
"Vaccinated or Idiot?"

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:07.234
[ Laughter ]
It's a fun game.

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:10.667
Some sports news --
baseball season is under way.

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:13.868
And I saw that despite --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:15.400
I'm excited.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.100
Despite warnings
from health experts,

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:22.267
the Texas Rangers had a full
crowd of more than 38,000 people

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:23.901
for their home opener.

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:25.467
Yeah, when they walked in,
all of the fans

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:28.267
got a Dr. Fauci bobblehead
that only shook its head no.

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:32.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.200
It was a strange game.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.467
It was the first time umpires

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:37.067
were trying to get themselves
thrown out.

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:41.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.300
Well, this is big.
March Madness has ended.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:44.968
And I want to say
congrats to Baylor

00:01:44.968 --> 00:01:48.200
for winning their first
men's basketball national title.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:54.300
Baylor played just like
Paul Rudd's entire life --

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.100
started off hot
and stayed that way.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.167
-Aw.
[ Applause ]

00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:59.133
-Happy birthday, Paul.

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:01.868
Of course, some of Baylor's
biggest alumni were in the game,

00:02:01.868 --> 00:02:04.067
including our friends
Chip and Joanna Gaines.

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:05.267
Here they are.

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:07.400
Yeah, it was a big night
for the Gaines family.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.567
Not only did their school win,
but after the game,

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:11.901
Joanna redid the entire court
in shiplap.

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:14.834
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.601
-Meanwhile, back on campus,

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:19.767
Baylor students celebrated
after the final buzzer.

00:02:19.767 --> 00:02:21.067
Watch this.

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:28.434
[ Cheering ]

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:29.968
-What?

00:02:29.968 --> 00:02:32.734
-Even the drunk dudes in Miami
were like, "That seems risky."

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:35.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:37.634
"I wouldn't do that."
-"Lucky I've had my --"

00:02:37.634 --> 00:02:41.567
-"You want to get on top of
that car and dance? Sure."

00:02:41.567 --> 00:02:42.767
Well, people were
talking about this.

00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:44.701
In response to
Coca-Cola opposing

00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:47.601
Georgia's new restrictive
voting law, President Trump

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:50.767
has told his supporters
to boycott the company.

00:02:50.767 --> 00:02:54.300
But check out this picture
taken in his office yesterday.

00:02:56.133 --> 00:02:59.300
Yeah. See it?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.667
-Come on.

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:04.400
-He has a bottle of Coke
on his desk. But don't worry.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.934
Trump fixed it by taking out
a Sharpie and writing "Pepsi."

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:08.968
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:10.601
-Could we also zoom
into the background

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:11.868
of his office for a second?

00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:13.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:16.267
Good Lord, how many bronze
Trumps does one office need?

00:03:16.267 --> 00:03:19.067
It's like, "Just give me
one more layer and perfect."

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:21.234
[ Laughter ]
"Perfect."

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:26.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.167
Some entertainment news --
I saw that there's going to be

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:31.267
an animated movie
based on marshmallow Peeps.

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:32.667
[ Laughter ]
-Ugh.

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:35.634
-Yep. The movie will be made now
but released in four years,

00:03:35.634 --> 00:03:37.367
just like the Peep
you ate at Easter.

00:03:37.367 --> 00:03:39.968
[ Laughter ]
-Oh!

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:42.667
Oh!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.667 --> 00:03:44.200
-Ah, Peeps movie.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.634
Right now, candy corn is like,

00:03:45.634 --> 00:03:46.901
"Oh, you think
you're better than us?"

00:03:46.901 --> 00:03:48.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:51.400
This is cool -- Last night
NFL quarterback Aaron Rodgers

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.767
made his guest-hosting debut
on "Jeopardy!"

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.834
Yep, Rodgers he did a great job,
but you could tell

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:58.367
he had some say in what
the categories would be.

00:03:58.367 --> 00:03:59.801
Watch this.

00:03:59.801 --> 00:04:02.701
-Let's get to the "Jeopardy!"
round with these categories.

00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:12.734
-Okay, okay, okay, we get it.
That's enough.

00:04:12.734 --> 00:04:13.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.934 --> 00:04:16.100
Get this -- A university
in Michigan is offering

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:17.667
a very unique scholarship.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:19.033
Check this out.

00:04:19.033 --> 00:04:21.734
-A Michigan university is
not only offering a degree

00:04:21.734 --> 00:04:25.200
in cannabis chemistry,
it's now the first university

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.200
in the nation to offer
a scholarship for it.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:31.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.400
-Yeah, it's a two-year program

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.234
that takes roughly 12 years
to complete.

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:41.367
[ Applause ]

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:45.300
Admission will be based on
combined scores from SATs, ACTs,

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.934
and THCs.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:49.834
That's right.
It's the only scholarship

00:04:49.834 --> 00:04:52.200
that comes with a year's supply
of Flamin' Hot Cheetos.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:55.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.334 --> 00:04:57.300
It's exciting on day one
when like,

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.200
"Please meet the new head
of the cannabis board,

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:00.767
Professor William Nelson."

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:02.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.667
"When you graduate, you move
your braid to the left."

00:05:04.667 --> 00:05:10.667
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.667 --> 00:05:13.167
That's a new joke, right?
-Come on, man.

00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:15.467
-Yeah, no one's made that joke.
-Willie Nelson's got braids.

00:05:15.467 --> 00:05:17.767
-Out of all of the Willie Nelson
jokes, no one's made that.

00:05:17.767 --> 00:05:19.100
-Willie Nelson known
for his love of cannabis.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.100
-First time it was ever made.
Yeah. Thank you, Higgins.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:22.300
-I didn't think
that got enough love.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:23.901
-Thank you. No, it did.
It got more than enough.

00:05:23.901 --> 00:05:24.868
Thank you.
-Oh, alright.

00:05:24.868 --> 00:05:27.634
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:29.234
It's still getting love now.

00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:31.167
-Yeah, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:32.434
-Well, this is strange.

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:35.534
I heard about a prison
in Montana that's open

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:38.033
to the public
for a very interesting activity.

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:39.133
Listen to this.

00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:40.601
-Brave people
can spend the night

00:05:40.601 --> 00:05:42.033
at an old Montana prison.

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:43.934
People can stay
for a ghost hunt.

00:05:43.934 --> 00:05:46.300
It lasts from 8:00 p.m.
to 5:00 a.m.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:48.601
They say not everyone is
guaranteed to see a ghost.

00:05:48.601 --> 00:05:51.634
It depends on the energy
that that person brings.

00:05:51.634 --> 00:05:54.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:58.400
-Hey, Jimmy, I think a spirit
from that Montana prison

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.367
is communicating with me now.

00:06:00.367 --> 00:06:02.167
-Oh, really?
What -- What's it saying?

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:04.567
-Well, it says -- Just a second.

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:05.734
Oh, yeah.

00:06:05.734 --> 00:06:07.601
It's saying,
"All the guests for this

00:06:07.601 --> 00:06:10.200
are going to be
probably white people."

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:15.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:15.667 --> 00:06:18.334
-I'm with you. I agree.

00:06:18.334 --> 00:06:21.200
I want to go. That sounds fun.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:24.767
And finally, a former Southwest
Airlines pilot is in trouble

00:06:24.767 --> 00:06:28.300
for exposing himself
during a flight.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:30.434
The pilot justified his actions
by saying

00:06:30.434 --> 00:06:32.801
his pants had been put on
a no-fly list.

